# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated output — disposable, reproducible, and never committed (CLAUDE.md §8.4)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
build/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# The SRS PDF is built from docs/SRS-v2.md by docs/build-pdf.sh.
# The Markdown is the source of truth; the PDF is a 1.6 MB artifact of it.
*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A real person's health data — NEVER commit this. (CLAUDE.md §8.4)
# The Garmin export is a teammate's actual sleep and activity record.
# Test fixtures are DERIVED from it, hand-written, and committed;
# the export itself is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.fit
garmin-export/
data/raw/
**/garmin_*.csv
**/garmin_*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI agent configuration — SHARED vs PERSONAL
#
# CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the team's shared rulebook and
# is loaded automatically by every session, so a rule added by one person
# reaches everyone else's agent on their next `git pull`. A rule that lives in
# three separate local copies is not a rule.
#
# Same for .claude/settings.json — hooks and permissions that must apply to
# everyone belong in version control. Only the *.local.json overrides, which
# hold one person's machine-specific choices, stay out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Syncthing conflict files — this repo lives outside the synced tree, but if a
# copy ever ends up inside one, these must not be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sync-conflict-*
